  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">We Effect - &#xe5;terintegrering Colombia 2022-2026 - We Effect-Reincorporation Colombia 2022-2026</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">We Effect-Reincorporation Colombia 2022-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektst&#xf6;det till We Effect i Colombia syftar till att underl&#xe4;tta &#xe5;terintegreringsprocessen f&#xf6;r kvinnliga och manliga f&#xf6;re-detta soldater tillsammans med deras grannkommuner, genom att genomf&#xf6;ra h&#xe5;llbara ekonomiska modeller baserade p&#xe5; kooperativa modeller med ett j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsperspektiv. St&#xf6;det &#xe4;r geografiskt inriktat p&#xe5; Montes de Maria-regionen (Sucre, Bolivar och Cordoba), som alla &#xe4;r konfliktdrabbade regioner. Detta st&#xf6;d &#xe4;r en andra fas av en tidigare insats f&#xf6;r &#xe5;terintegreringsprocessen med ID-nummer: 12204.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project support to We Effect in Colombia has the objective to facilitate the reincorporation process of female and male ex-combatants jointly with their neighbouring communities, through the implementation of sustainable economic models based on cooperative models with gender perspective included. The contribution has its geographical focus in the Montes de Maria region (Sucre, Bolivar, and Cordoba), which are conflict-affected regions. This contribution is a second phase, building on a previous contribution to the reincorporation process with ID-number: 12204</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed impact goal is: Sustainable rural development, resilient to climate change, with gender justice and using cooperative models, which reinforce territorial roots and contribute to the reconstruction of the social fabric and a peaceful society in Colombia.&quot;

The outcome goal is men and women ex-combatants in a reincorporation process together with their neighboring communities, implementing sustainable economic models, based on cooperative models and with a gender perspective, guaranteeing access to rights and participation in peace building. The specific objective slightly changed from the concept note, focusing on a specific region.  The new proposed specific objective is: men and women ex-combatants in a reincorporation process part of social and solidarity economic organizations from municipalities of the Departments of Bol&#xed;var, Sucre and C&#xf3;rdoba, their families and communities participate to improve their socioeconomic conditions and help in building peace.

The following three specific outputs are proposed:

1. The women ex-combatants in a reincorporation process from the organizations and communities of the municipalities of Bol&#xed;var, Sucre and C&#xf3;rdoba have strengthened their political and economic empowerment and their capacities to recognize and exercise their rights.

2. Women&apos;s and mixed organizations, ex-combatants in a reincorporation process, from the social and solidarity economy in municipalities of Bol&#xed;var, Sucre and C&#xf3;rdoba, have comprehensively developed and improved sustainable enterprises leveraged by capital, financial inclusion, knowledge management, associativity, alliances and including the gender approach.

3. Organizations, their families and communities in municipalities in Bol&#xed;var, Sucre and C&#xf3;rdoba, particularly women and youth, influence public policies to gain access to rights and help strengthen coexistence and local and regional reconciliation.</narrative>
  </description>
